}=-4 \\\\ -3{x}_{2}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${x}_{2}=-\\frac{2}{3}$ and ${x}_{1}=2.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, ${y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=-4+3(-\\frac{2}{3})=-6.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377100 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186377101 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377100 #edb/ref 1069 "q-32543" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377100 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377100 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $3\\times 3$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377100 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bf45deeb-ab83-510b-8f67-2f8280e43963" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377100 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=1 \\\\ -2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-2 \\\\ -{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}+{y}_{3}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the solution to this system using forward substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & =1, \\\\ {y}_{2} & =-2+2{y}_{1} \\\\  & =-2+2(1) \\\\  & =0, \\\\ {y}_{3} & =2+{y}_{1}-{y}_{2} \\\\  & =2+(1)-(0) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere